  "answer": "All changes are in place. Let me do a final review of the requirements against my implementation:\n\n**Requirements checklist:**\n\n1. ✅ `dispatch(path)` is the entry point, returns `{ route, params }`.\n2. ✅ Invalid paths (not string, empty, not starting with `/`) throw `TypeError` — handled in `resolveFromRegistry` which `dispatch` delegates to.\n3. ✅ Pathname text unchanged: case-sensitive (`===` for static, exact segment compare for dynamic), trailing slash distinct (segment count/emptiness checks).\n4. ✅ Route ID is a string; `params` is a new plain object each call.\n5. ✅ Default routes from `fixtures/routes.mjs` used by `dispatch`.\n6. ✅ `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)` uses same matching policy.\n7. ✅ Static wins over dynamic regardless of declaration order (collect both, prefer static).\n8. ✅ First matching dynamic wins (only set if `dynamicMatch === null`).\n9. ✅ Fallback only if neither matched.\n10. ✅ First declared static wins; first declared fallback wins.\n11. ✅ No match + no fallback → `null`.\n12. ✅ No mutation of records; returned values independent (fresh objects).\n13. ✅ `legacyResolve` in `legacy.mjs` unchanged, still handles `/old/help`.\n14. ✅ Adapters/utilities untouched.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n- **`entry.mjs`**: Removed the incorrect `legacyResolve` call from `dispatch`. `dispatch` now delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`, so the production entry point uses the production route table with the correct matching policy (and inherits input validation).\n\n- **`registry.mjs`**: Rewrote `resolveFromRegistry` to implement the specified matching policy:\n  - Validates the path (throws `TypeError` for non-string, empty, or non-`/`-prefixed input).\n  - Scans all records once, capturing the first matching static, the first matching dynamic, and the first fallback independently — instead of returning on the first record encountered.\n  - Returns static over dynamic regardless of declaration order, then dynamic, then fallback, else `null`.\n  - Builds fresh `params` objects so results are independent of later calls and records are never mutated.\n\nThe dynamic matcher (`routes/dynamic.mjs`), static matcher, fallback helper, `legacy.mjs`, adapters, and utilities already conformed to their specs and were left unchanged.",
